secrets.yml
# Glob form, not `.history/`: a directory-level ignore prunes the whole
# subtree before git ever evaluates the negations below, so `!.history/*.md`
# would be silently dead (git can't re-include a file whose parent dir is
# excluded). Keep this as `.history/*` or the negations stop working again.
.history/*
.torrent-cache
*.log
# Negate the intentionally-tracked files by EXACT NAME, not by `*.md`/`*.sh`
# glob (#591). This directory holds raw operator command logs - real IPs,
# hostnames, full command output, written under a "git-ignored so it's safe"
# assumption (.history/README.md) - and this repo is public. A glob negation
# means a plain `git add -A` stages every new log; there were 21 untracked
# ones when #591 was swept. Same shape as the .a5c/processes block below:
# tracking is opt-in per file, anything new stays local. A write-up that
# really belongs in git goes to docs/ or .github/instructions/, not here.
!.history/README.md
!.history/USAGE.md
!.history/log-cmd.sh
!.history/shell-functions.sh
!.history/start-logged-session.sh
!.history/2026-05-17-wg-hop-lxc-setup.md
!.history/2026-05-17-wg-hop-public-exposure.md
raid-migration
.claude/
# Babysitter (.a5c) — best-practice (BEST-PRACTICES.md): track institutional
# knowledge (.a5c/processes/, .a5c/project-profile.json/.md) by NOT ignoring it;
# ignore only noisy/large/sensitive artifacts. Cannot use a blanket `.a5c/`
# because git can't re-include children of a wholly-excluded directory.
.a5c/node_modules/
.a5c/runs/
.a5c/logs/
.a5c/cache/
.a5c/inputs/
.a5c/package-lock.json
.a5c/creds.env
.a5c/creds.env.tmp.*

# Sensitive data - database dumps, backups, research extracts with credentials
2-k3s/08.servarr/_backups/postgres-dumps/
2-k3s/08.servarr/_backups/sqlite-zips/
2-k3s/08.servarr/_backups/postgres-schemas-*/
2-k3s/08.servarr/research/app-configs.xml
2-k3s/08.servarr/research/truenas-configs.txt
2-k3s/08.servarr/research/truenas-ix-apps-full.txt
*.sql
*.sql.gz
*.zip

# Local cache from kustomize+helm pull (per-Application 2-k3s/0X.*/charts/)
charts/

# SOPS plaintext drafts — never commit. Always encrypt to *.enc.yaml first.
*-plaintext.yaml
*.plaintext.yaml
# #659: the per-file negation block that used to live here (`.a5c/processes/*`
# + 11 `!` negations) regrew the exact opt-in trap it copied from .history -
# only the files someone remembered to negate stayed tracked, so 143 of 154
# real process definitions went untracked and invisible to git (PR #110/#111
# swept it once, it fully regrew). Unlike .history, these files hold no real
# IPs/secrets (checked before dropping the ignore), so there is no reason to
# opt in per file. Track everything under .a5c/processes/ by default, same as
# the top-of-block comment always intended. Drift is now caught by the
# pre-commit guard (.github/hooks/check-processes-tracked.sh) instead of by
# a gitignore negation list nobody updates.

# Superpowers subagent-driven-development scratch (ledger, briefs, review packages).
# Per-plan workspaces under .superpowers/sdd/<plan>/ — the git history is the record.
.superpowers/

# Compose .env files hold runtime secrets (AirVPN account password, Cloudflare
# tunnel tokens) for the user-VM stacks. Never commit these.
.env
*.env
!*.env.example

# Playwright MCP scratch - browser snapshots, which can capture account pages.
.playwright-mcp/

# Python bytecode. images/vpn-picker/ is the repo's only Python source; running
# its selftest locally drops a __pycache__ next to it.
__pycache__/

# Scratch triage notes (#662) - per-issue investigation notes and baseline/
# before-state captures written while working an issue. Unlike .history/,
# NO tracked exceptions: the GitHub issue/PR they feed is the durable record,
# and at least one baseline capture already carried a raw show title (banned
# per this repo's rule on media names in committed git). Convention documented
# in general.instructions.md.
artifacts/
